Package: HrankdCov
Type: Package
Title: Distribution-Free Tests of Multivariate Independence via
    Center-Outward Ranks
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Hongjian", "Shi", , "hongjian.shi@tum.de", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-5552-2082"))
Description: Computes the center-outward ranks and signs of Hallin, del
    Barrio, Cuesta-Albertos and Matrán (2021) <doi:10.1214/20-AOS1996>,
    obtained by optimally assigning the data to a regular grid in the unit
    ball, and uses them to test independence between two random vectors
    of arbitrary dimensions.  The test statistic is the distance
    covariance of (scored) center-outward ranks, as proposed by Shi, Drton
    and Han (2022) <doi:10.1080/01621459.2020.1782223> and Shi, Hallin,
    Drton and Han (2022) <doi:10.1214/21-AOS2151>.  The resulting tests are
    consistent and fully distribution-free.  P-values are computed from
    the exact (permutation) null distribution, which does not depend on
    the data-generating distribution and can be reused across tests, or
    from the limiting weighted chi-square distribution.
